B.BD=new A.b7(B.BW,["Welcome","Your family deserves a written plan","Plan language","Choose your language","Language","Continue","Cancel","How to read this plan","Your plan is ready","View dashboard","My Dashboard","My Dashboard \xb7 Wallet & Progress","Monthly SIP","Primary SIP needed","Continue your SIP for {y} years","Target","{p}% funded","Due by {y}","/month","Costs today","In {y} yrs (with inflation)","starts at age {a}","Child Education","Marriage","Dream Home","Retirement","Legacy","Custom Goal","Talk to your Relationship Manager","Edit Inputs","BOOK \xb7 CALL NOW","WHATSAPP US","Download PDF Report","Copy Plan","Delete Saved Plan","Tour this plan","Save plan","Your Money Score","Needs attention","Getting stronger","Strong","Savings","Emergency fund","Insurance","Debt load","Investment mix","Goal readiness","This pillar weighs most on your score","Retirement readiness","Freedom year","Corpus covers annual expenses","Child future planner","Goal progress tracker","Early Starter","Starting now is your biggest advantage \u2014 compounding does the heavy lifting. Protect income, automate SIPs, keep learning.","Right On Time","This is the sweet spot: enough runway for wealth, enough income to act fast. Lock insurance early and step up SIPs yearly.","Accelerate Now","No panic \u2014 but no pause either. Raise savings rate, trim low-yield debt, and protect the family first; growth follows.","Protect & Compound","Priority shifts to protection and certainty: adequate cover, controlled risk, and disciplined withdrawals planning ahead.","Tip of the day","For salaried planners","Check EPF/NPS headroom and 80C usage once a year; automate SIPs on salary day; keep 6 months of expenses liquid.","For business owners","Keep business and family money in separate accounts, provision taxes quarterly, and hold a larger emergency buffer.","For every planner","Review insurance yearly, step up SIPs with every increment, and rebalance when any asset sleeve drifts \xb110%.","Confirm your details","One quick check before we run your numbers \u2014 make sure everything below is right.","Run my plan","Edit","Name","Age","Monthly income","Monthly expenses","Existing EMIs","Occupation","Salaried","Business","Self-employed / Professional","Other","SIP","years","L","Cr","Your Family Deserves More Than a Calculator.","It deserves a financial plan.","We'll understand your family, your responsibilities, your current finances and the dreams you want to achieve.","Choose your language \xb7 \u0905\u092a\u0928\u0940 \u092d\u093e\u0937\u093e \u091a\u0941\u0928\u0947\u0902","This usually takes 7\u201310 minutes.","Don't worry about exact numbers. Approximate figures are perfectly fine.","Let's Build My Plan \u2192","I'll complete it later","Switch usage mode","Building your family plan","Family","Money","Goals","Protection","Plan","Section {a} of {b}","Editing your saved plan \u2014 goal costs, dependents & assumptions are adjustable; everything else stays locked.","Back","Continue","See My Plan","years","{n} years","Why do we ask?","Your plan, dashboard and PDF are personalised with your name \u2014 it is your family\u2019s story, after all.","Age decides the time available for every goal \u2014 and time is the biggest input in every calculation.","We ask this because the time available before the goal determines how much you need to prepare.","Income sets the upper boundary of what the plan can safely commit every month.","Expenses tell us how much is truly free for goals \u2014 realistic numbers make realistic plans.","EMIs are commitments already made. We subtract them so the plan never over-promises your surplus.","This helps us understand how much money is immediately available if something unexpected happens.","We ask this so the plan considers the protection you already have \u2014 no double counting.","Existing health cover is counted first; the plan then suggests only the real gap.","The start year decides how long your money gets to grow \u2014 and how long it must last.","A rough today-cost is enough. The engine projects it with assumed inflation and builds the roadmap.","What matters most to your family?","Select the things you would like your financial plan to prepare for.","Emergency Fund","Money for life's unexpected moments","Children's Education","Help your children pursue the future they choose","Children's Marriage","Prepare for their special day without financial pressure","Retirement","Build the freedom to live comfortably after work","Home / Land","Work towards your dream property","Car / Vehicle","Plan for the vehicle your family wants","Travel","Make important family experiences possible","Family Legacy","Create wealth for the next generation","Your Own Goals","Write any other goal \u2014 a cost & year card opens for it.","e.g. Startup Fund, World Tour, Farm House","Add","Your Family Plan","Monthly surplus","Your financial plan is taking shape.","Let's start with your family","Every financial plan begins with one simple question \u2014 who are we planning this money for?","What should we call you?","Your name","How old are you?","Would you like to include your spouse/partner?","Yes","No","Their name","Name","Their age","Who depends on your family income?","Your plan should protect the people who depend on you today \u2014 and prepare for the children who will depend on you tomorrow.","Do you financially support parents or other adults?","Use \u2212 / + to tell us how many","Person {n}","Who are they?","Father","Mother","Other","Name / Nickname","e.g., Maa \xb7 Papa","Age","Tell us about your children","Each child gets their own education and celebration goals \u2014 by name.","+ Add a child","+ Add another child","No dependents? Just hit Continue.","Child {n}","What should we call your child?","Name / Nickname","This is my:","Son","Daughter","Son","Daughter","Father","Mother","Family member","Child","Let's understand your monthly money flow","You don't need exact figures. A realistic estimate is enough.","How much money comes into your family each month?","How much does your family spend each month?","Ideal household expenses: about {v} (70% of income). Expenses must stay less than income.","Do you currently have any loans or EMIs?","Add the total EMI you pay every month. Enter 0 if there is none.","How much money can you access immediately if something unexpected happens?","Include your bank balance and any liquid money you can access quickly.","Your current monthly surplus","Based on what you've entered, around {v} may currently be available each month for future goals, protection and investments.","Right now expenses and EMIs exceed income \u2014 your plan will honestly highlight this gap and how to close it.","Income","Expenses + EMIs","Potential surplus","Before building wealth, let's protect it.","A strong financial plan should continue even when life doesn't go according to plan.","What best describes your work?","Self-employed","How much life insurance do you already have?","Add the total cover across your existing life or term policies.","How much health insurance does your family already have? (in lakh)","Add the total health cover available across your family policies.","Protection Check","We'll compare your existing protection with your family's income, responsibilities and future goals. The detailed recommendation appears in your final plan.","\ud83c\udf93 Let's plan for {n}'s future","{n} is {age} today. If higher education begins around age {ga}, you have approximately {yrs} years to prepare.","For {n}, age {age} \u2014 this goal is due now.","What kind of education are you considering?","Other / Custom","Custom education name","e.g. Pilot Training, Design School","Today's estimated cost","What could this cost in the future?","At an assumed {inf}% inflation.","The good news is that you don't need {fv} today. You have {yrs} years to build this goal gradually.","\ud83d\udc8d Let\u2019s prepare for a special day","{n}'s Marriage \xb7 Today you may be thinking about school, hobbies and childhood. One day, you'll be preparing for one of the biggest celebrations of their life.","Today's estimated cost","Estimated future cost","Time available","{yrs} years gives this goal something extremely valuable \u2014 time.","\ud83c\udf05 Let's plan for the life you want after work","Retirement isn't simply about stopping work. It's about having the freedom to live without depending on a salary.","When would you like your retirement income to begin?","How much would you need every month in today\u2019s money?","Enter 0 to skip this goal.","Estimated monthly need at {age}","Estimated retirement corpus","Your biggest advantage today is time. The earlier you start, the more time your money has to work for you.","Today's estimated cost","When would you like this? (years from now)","At an assumed {inf}% inflation, this becomes {fv} in {yrs} years.","Work towards your dream property \u2014 a budget and a year is all we need.","The upgrade your family has in mind \u2014 rough budget, target year.","One big family experience \u2014 what would it cost today, and when?","Your own goal \u2014 set the budget and the year.","Wealth to leave behind by age {age}. Your retirement corpus counts toward this \u2014 we plan only the gap.","Legacy fund target (today's value)","At an assumed {inf}% inflation \u2192 {fv} by age {age}.","Let's make sure we've got your story right.","One quick read-through \u2014 tap Edit beside anything you want to change.","Family","Children","Monthly finances","Goals","Edit","Income","Expenses","EMI","Available savings","Monthly surplus","No children added","No goals selected yet","{n}'s Education","{n}'s Marriage","Everything looks good? A few planning defaults are next \u2014 then your plan.","Review Assumptions","These defaults are the basis of every future value, corpus and SIP \u2014 confirm them, or fine-tune right here before we compute your roadmap.","Standard Inflation","Equity Return (p.a.)","Debt Return (p.a.)","Equity / Debt Allocation","Manual allocation \u2014 equity + debt always equals 100%","Auto from the 100 \u2212 age rule ({auto}% equity at age {age})","Education at {a}","Marriage at {a}","Pension from {a}","Legacy by {a}","Fine-tune ages & more","Your family's story is almost complete.","We've understood where your family stands today, what matters to you and what you want to achieve tomorrow. Now let's turn those dreams into a clear financial roadmap.","Everything you told us is about to become one clear plan.","Everything you told us, {n}, is about to become one clear plan.","Sign in once with Google and we compute your full roadmap \u2014 goals, protection, SIPs and a premium PDF report. Your plan follows your login on every device.","Create My Family Financial Plan \u2192","Monthly income must be more than zero.","Expenditure can't be negative.","Expenses must be less than income \u2014 ideally about 70% of income.","Please tell us your name.","Age should be between 18 and 80.","Please enter your partner's name \u2014 or tap No above.","Partner age should be between 18 and 100.","Please name every dependent adult.","Adult dependent age should be 18\u2013100.","Please name every child.","Please choose Son or Daughter for every child.","Child age should be 0\u201340."],t.l)
